{"skill":{"slug":"focus-deep-work","displayName":"Focus Deep Work"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769326446742,"changelog":"Initial release of Focus & Deep Work.\n\n- Introduces guided focus sessions with Pomodoro, Ultradian, and custom timers.\n- Enables distraction logging without interrupting workflow.\n- Provides productivity tracking with session summaries and weekly/monthly statistics.\n- Automates environment setup (notifications silenced, apps blocked, etc.) for distraction-free work.\n- All data stored locally—no cloud syncing or server uploads.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3691,"sha256":"49210c4f52887892fb0885a009ca2c44fcfcd224764087191f8b121ff7d9647f","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1757,"sha256":"66ff09a98f904f238d79da3f0204a5fb0f769ee0042cdd4d3849f3e65311ffc7","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789017930869,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"348bd3ddb1851e24d2397f9deb70d8ac35694fe6d80d5c1b7803656fb74268a1","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/348bd3ddb1851e24d2397f9deb70d8ac35694fe6d80d5c1b7803656fb74268a1","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: focus-deep-work\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle is classified as benign. The `SKILL.md` clearly describes its purpose: to enhance focus through features like app blocking, notification silencing, and website blocking. While these are powerful system-level actions, they are explicitly stated as core functionalities of the 'focus-deep-work' skill and are qualified with 'when permissions allow' or 'if permission granted'. There is no evidence of prompt injection attempts against the AI agent, no instructions for unauthorized data access, and the documentation explicitly states, 'All data stays local on your machine,' negating data exfiltration concerns.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159910386},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":22,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":3,"checkedAt":1789017930869},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a disclosed focus-session helper with local tracking and optional device-setting changes, with no executable code or hidden data flow found.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Changing notifications, brightness, app state, or website access is proportionate to a focus-mode skill, and the artifact discloses these behaviors as permission-dependent.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact contains only a single Markdown skill file and no install scripts, dependencies, executable payloads, or remote retrieval instructions.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Some trigger phrases are broad or colloquial, so a user should make sure disruptive actions such as app blocking or do-not-disturb changes are confirmed before execution.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill describes local session history and focus statistics, but no cross-session backdoor, background service, credential use, privilege escalation, or external transmission.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is deep-work assistance, and the described capabilities fit that purpose: timers, distraction logging, productivity summaries, notification silencing, app or website blocking, and focus music.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing, verify that the agent asks before muting notifications, blocking sites, closing or minimizing apps, or changing brightness. The reviewed artifact says focus data stays local and contains no executable code.","findings":"[TR2] expected: The 'start focus' trigger is somewhat generic, but it is plainly related to the skill purpose and does not indicate hidden or unrelated behavior.\n[SQP-1] expected: The frontmatter triggers are broad natural-language focus phrases; this is a usability and accidental-activation concern, not evidence of malicious behavior.\n[SQP-1] expected: The usage examples include phrases like 'Minimize distractions' and 'Lock me in'; because the resulting actions can affect the device environment, confirmation would be prudent.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789017930869}}}}}